  "output_text": "**Results**  \n\n**Introduction/Context**  \nTumor-infiltrating plasma cells (clusters 7-10) were analyzed via scRNA-seq across 7 cancer types. Four clusters were annotated using differentially expressed genes (DEGs) and pathway enrichments.  \n\n**Keywords**  \nPlasma cells, tumor microenvironment, immunoglobulin, heat shock proteins, metallothioneins, stress response.  \n\n**Candidate Genes**  \nIGHA2, IGKC2, HSPA6, HSPA1B, MT2A1, MT1X1, IGLV6-57, IGKV4-1.  \n\n**Pathway Enrichments**  \n**Cluster 7 (Plasma cells):**  \n- **Top Upregulated Pathways**: B cell receptor signaling (IGHV/IGKV/IGLV genes), antigen processing/presentation.  \n- **Leading Genes**: IGLV6-57 (avg_log2FC 3.23), IGKV4-1 (3.22).  \n\n**Cluster 8 (Plasma cells):**  \n- **Top Upregulated Pathways**: Unfolded protein response (HSPA6, HSPA1B), stress granule formation.  \n- **Leading Genes**: HSPA6 (6.65), HSPA1B (4.01).  \n\n**Cluster 9 (Plasma cells):**  \n- **Top Upregulated Pathways**: Immunoglobulin secretion (IGHA2, IGKC2), mucosal immunity.  \n- **Leading Genes**: IGHA2 (1.87), IGKC2 (1.41).  \n\n**Cluster 10 (Plasma cells):**  \n- **Top Upregulated Pathways**: Metal detoxification (MT2A1, MT1X1), oxidative stress response.  \n- **Leading Genes**: MT2A1 (4.57), MT1X1 (4.07).  \n\n**Targeted Subset Analysis**  \n- **Immunoglobulin-Related Clusters**: Clusters 7 (IGKV/IGLV), 9 (IGHA2/IGKC2) reflect distinct antibody-producing subsets.  \n- **Stress-Response Clusters**: Cluster 8 (HSPA6/HSPA1B) and 10 (MT2A1/MT1X1) highlight divergent stress adaptation mechanisms.  \n\n**Key Genes/Proteins (Leading Edge)**  \n**Upregulated**:  \n| Gene     | Direction | Role/Function               | Pathway(s)                |  \n|----------|-----------|-----------------------------|---------------------------|  \n| IGHV/IGK | Up        | Antigen recognition         | BCR signaling             |  \n| HSPA6    | Up        | Protein folding             | Unfolded protein response |  \n| MT2A1    | Up        | Metal detoxification        | Oxidative stress          |  \n\n**Comparisons**  \n- **Cluster 7 vs. 9**: Both express immunoglobulins but differ in isotype (IGLV/KV vs. IGHA2/IGKC2), suggesting functional divergence in antibody specificity.  \n- **Cluster 8 vs. 10**: Distinct stress pathways (heat shock vs. metallothionein) imply non-redundant roles in tumor microenvironment adaptation.  \n\n**Implications**  \n- Stress-response clusters (8, 10) may contribute to plasma cell survival in harsh tumor environments.  \n- Cluster 9’s IgA2 expression suggests a role in mucosal tumor immunity (e.g., gastrointestinal cancers).  \n\n**Next Steps**  \n1. Validate functional roles of HSPA6/MT2A1 in plasma cell stress tolerance via CRISPR screens.  \n2. Assess spatial localization of Cluster 9 IgA+ plasma cells in mucosal tumors.  \n3. Compare immunoglobulin repertoire diversity between Clusters 7 and 9.  \n\n**Rationale**  \nAssignments are based on DEGs and literature on plasma cell biology. Absence of external datasets limits mechanistic inference.",
